{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.SemistandardTableau","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.NumSYTPos"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitMatrix_braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitMatrix_braid_relation","kind":"axiom","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Hoefsmit.lean#L152-L165","doc":"**Braid relation** (axiomatised): `T_i T_{i+1} T_i = T_{i+1}\nT_i T_{i+1}` whenever both `i` and `i+1` index valid\ngenerators (`i+1 < n - 1`).\n\nThis is the T-form braid relation matching the T-form Hecke\nrelation `T_i^2 = (q − 1) T_i + q` above.  The braid relation\nhas the same shape as the σ-form (it does not depend on the\nquadratic relation), but we phrase it in T's to keep this\nfile uniformly in the T-form / `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`-friendly setup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitMatrix_hecke_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitMatrix_hecke_relation","kind":"axiom","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Hoefsmit.lean#L121-L150","doc":"**Hecke relation in T-form** (the F_p-friendly form, per\nuser direction \"we want as many stmts to hold in F_p\"):\n\n    `T_i² = (q − 1) · T_i + q · 1`\n\nINTEGER coefficients in q ⟹ holds uniformly across all F_p\nwhen `q : ZMod p`.  The σ-form alternative\n`σ_i² = (q^{1/2} − q^{−1/2}) σ_i + 1` requires `q^{1/2}` and\ntherefore lives over `ℚ(q^{1/2})` — losing F_p compatibility\nat primes where `q^{1/2}` doesn't exist.\n\nConversion: `T_i = q^{1/2} σ_i` (in σ-form), so the two\nformulations are related by a `q^{1/2}` rescaling that we\navoid by working in T-form throughout.\n\nNOTE: previous draft (post-Gemini-review) used σ-form.\nReverted to T-form because:\n1. F_p compatibility (per user direction).\n2. The Mathlib-port aligns naturally with `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`.\n3. The σ-form's `q^{1/2}` necessitates `ℚ(q^{1/2})` which\n   has poor F_p reduction properties.\n\nFor the q-integer convention, the T-form analogue is\n`[k]_q := (q^k − 1) / (q − 1)` (a polynomial in q, integer\ncoefficients).  See `QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitMatrix","kind":"opaque","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Hoefsmit.lean#L111-L119","doc":"**Hoefsmit seminormal matrix** for generator `σ_i` of\n`H_n(q)` acting on the irrep `V_λ` at parameter `q`.\n\nAxiomatised at the type level pending the Mathlib port of\nHoefsmit (1974); the concrete construction is in\n`computations/hecke/hecke_characters.py`\n(function `build_seminormal_matrices`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.seminormalDim_pos'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.seminormalDim_pos'","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Hoefsmit.lean#L107-L109","doc":"Positivity of `f^λ` without the unused nonemptiness hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.seminormalDim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.seminormalDim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Hoefsmit.lean#L91-L105","doc":"The seminormal dimension is positive.\n\n**Was a cited `axiom`; now proved (2026-09-03).** `f^λ = Nat.card` of a type\nthat is `Finite` (injective encoding) and `Nonempty` (the row-superstandard\ntableau, sorry-free in `QOU/BraidKnot/SytRowSuperstandard.lean`), so\n`Nat.card_pos` applies.\n\nThe `0 < n` hypothesis is **retained for compatibility but unused**: the\nempty diagram carries exactly one standard tableau — the empty one — so the\ncount is `1`, and positivity is unconditional. `seminormalDim_pos'` below is\nthe hypothesis-free form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.seminormalDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit.seminormalDim","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Hoefsmit.lean#L79-L89","doc":"The seminormal dimension of the irrep `V_λ` — equal to `f^λ`, the number of\nstandard Young tableaux of shape `λ`.\n\n**No longer opaque (2026-09-03).** This was `opaque`, with the docstring\n*\"axiomatised pending the Mathlib `StandardYoungTableau` enumeration\"*. That\nenumeration exists: `QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux` counts the\nin-repo standard-tableau type Mathlib lacks, and `QOU.Mathlib.dimSYT` is\nexactly `f^λ` for a partition's shape. The stated blocker had been cleared;\nnobody came back to the definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}